d Hiring How to Recruit and Hire Assessment and Intake Post and Recruit Post and Recruit Overview Pay History Requirements for Pay and Benefit Information in Job Postings VEVRAA Screen and Select Offer and Accept Hiring Letter Templates Hiring Guidance by Employee Type Hiring Student Employees Hiring Temporary or Casual Employees Hiring Academic Employees Hiring Executive Employees Managing Time and Absences Work. With Flexibility. Overview: Work. With Flexibility. Best Practices for Implementation Best Practices for Flexible Work Implementation Sample Implementation Plans: Work. With Flexibility. Flexible Work Options Supervisor Support Work. With Flexibility FAQs Managing Performance and Development Performance Management Great Goals, Great Performance How to reward, recognize, and encourage strong performance Ongoing Check-Ins Performance Appraisal Tool (PAT) Performance Evaluations Performance Evaluation Policies Performance Evaluation Tips Dealing with Performance Problems Dealing with Performance Issues Facilitated Meetings Collaborative Approach to Problem Solving Problem-Solving Outline Document and Communicate Responsibilities, Goals, and Objectives Employee Engagement The Employee Engagement Cycle The Employee Engagement Survey Support Survey Participation Navigate the Dashboard View and Export Results Survey Comments Interpret Survey Results Systemwide Results and Response Rates Lead Discussions Take Action Understanding GA Roles & Fellowships Managing Student Employees Offboarding HR PEAK HR PEAK Services HR PEAK Training Departing Employees Professional Development Employee Development Center EDC Overview Gigs Mentorship Leading on All Levels Supervisory and Leadership Development Supervisory and Leadership Development Supervisory Development Program Leadership Competencies and Assessments Leadership Competencies Overview The Leadership Competency Framework Assessment Options Self-Assessment 360 Degree Assessments Options Overview Development Stakeholder Academic Leader Center Director Leadership Consulting Services EDI Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion in the Workplace Work with Our EDI Team Intercultural Development Inventory (IDI®) Discussion Toolkits University Partners HR Inclusion in Practice About OHR Mission and Vision OHR Directory HR Updates OHR Events Breadcrumb Home Benefits Discounts and Perks U Perks for Faculty and Staff U Perks for Faculty and Staff Main navigation Discounts and Perks U Perks for Faculty and Staff Tuition Benefits Expand Tuition Benefits menu About the Regents Tuition Benefits Program How to Use the Regents Tuition Benefit Program University of Minnesota faculty and staff enjoy unique discounts and opportunities as employees. University Discounts Expand all + Tuition Discount at the U of M for Employees Expand your education. The Regents Tuition Benefit Program helps pay employee tuition when they take University courses. Between 75% to 100% percent of tuition costs are covered for undergraduate, graduate school, or post baccalaureate professional course credits. + Discounts on Laptops and Tablets M Tech —located in the Bookstore at Coffman Memorial Union—offers special savings to University employees on technology products. Qualified staff and faculty can take advantage of payroll deduction for select technology purchases. + Professional Development Office of Human Resources (OHR) Professional Development Opportunities offer free and flexible learning opportunities, mentorship, and training opportunities to help staff and faculty grow skills, explore new career paths, and lead with confidence. Carlson Executive Education is pleased to offer a 50% discount to University of Minnesota faculty and staff on its programs. Discounted enrollment is limited and subject to space availability. For more information, please visit the UMN Faculty/Staff Discount Process page on the Carlson Executive Education website. College of Continuing and Professional Studies (CCAPS) offers staff and faculty members a 50% discount on most professional development courses, which cover a range of topics. + Boynton Pharmacy Discount Boynton Pharmacy offers University employees a 10% discount on over-the-counter products. Simply show your employee ID at checkout. The Boynton Pharmacy team also makes prescription transfers hassle-free and offers statewide mail delivery (MN and WI). Exclusions and mailing charges may apply. + Boynton Eye Clinic Discount The Boynton Health Eye Clinic offers all University employees a 20% discount on a complete pair of eyeglasses (frames and lenses). + YMCA Early Childhood Learning Center The YMCA Early Childhood Learning Center on the U of M Twin Cities campus offers high-quality full-day care and early education for children ages 6 weeks to Pre-K. University of Minnesota employee perk: 5% discount on YMCA Early Childhood tuition Programs available: Infants, Toddlers, Preschool and Pre-K Learn more and call for availability Unique University Offerings Expand all + Twin Cities Campus: Seasonal Fresh Food The Food Science and Nutrition Department's Dairy Food Products salesroom is open to the public. Seasonal offerings from the CFANS Market include organic produce from a student-run farm, honey, and Christmas trees. (Twin Cities Campus) + Museums and Galleries Explore University museums and galleries, including: University of Minnesota Duluth Tweed Museum of Art University of Minnesota Morris Edward J. & Helen Jane Morrison Gallery University of Minnesota Twin Cities Bell Museum of Natural History Goldstein Museum of Design Minnesota Landscape Arboretum Regis Center for Art The Raptor Center Weisman Art Museum Student Union & Activities (student-guided art galleries) + Student Athletic Events Watch student-athletes compete in nearly a dozen sports. Eligible Twin Cities faculty and staff can purchase discounted single-game tickets as well as discounted season tickets. Receive a 20% discount on season tickets and up to a 20% discount on single-game tickets. Single-game discounts are only available for home, regular-season events (subject to availability). The discount includes all ticketed varsity athletic events: Football Volleyball Soccer Men's & Women's Hockey Men's & Women's Basketball Wrestling Gymnastics Baseball Softball To be eligible, faculty and staff must have an appointment of 75% time or more. You can buy faculty or staff season or single-game tickets or get more information by contacting the Gopher Ticket Sales & Service Office at 1-800-U-GOPHER or emailing [email protected] . Learn more about accessing your discount . + Library Services All faculty and staff can use the campus libraries to get answers to questions, use online databases and streaming services, or check out materials and have them delivered to your workplace. + Northrop Ticket and Discounts Northrop offers world-class dance and music at the heart of the UMN Twin Cities campus. To be the first to know about event announcements, exclusive offers, discounts and presale codes, join the Email Club and follow along on Instagram and Facebook . Staff and Faculty are eligible for these discounts at Northrop : Take 20% off ticket prices with a Northrop Season subscription package of three or more season* events . Subscribe by Sept. 24, 2026. $20 Rush Tickets: Available two hours before some Northrop Season performances with a valid U Card (limit 2 tickets per person). Rush ticket availability will be posted on the event page of Northrop's website. UMN faculty and staff are invited to experience in-person/online Northrop Season* performances with their students, incorporating the work performed on stage with their classroom curriculum at no charge, through the Northrop Across Campus program. *Some exclusions apply. + Multiple Campuses: Rent Outdoor Gear for Your Next Adventure Outdoor equipment rentals are available for faculty and staff through the University Recreation and Wellness. You can find what you need to enjoy the Minnesota outdoors throughout the year, including tents, bikes, canoes, paddleboards, snowshoes, and cross-country skis. Available on the Crookston , Duluth , Morris , and Twin Cities campuses. + Companion Animal Teaching Clinic (CATC) University of Minnesota employees and students can access veterinary care for their cats and dogs through the Veterinary Medical Center’s Companion Animal Teaching Clinic (CATC) . Pets receive care from veterinary students in their clinical year under the supervision of faculty veterinarians and veterinary technicians. Services include wellness and sick-pet exams, vaccinations, diagnostic testing, select surgical procedures, specialty care referrals, and end-of-life support. Discounts Outside the University Expand all + Coursera for Minnesota Coursera for Minnesota gives University of Minnesota employees free access to more than 2,000 Coursera courses. Take any course you want, whenever you want. Learn new skills, explore a new subject, or advance your career goals. Note: Coursera courses do not provide U of M academic credit unless used as part of a regular class. For information about accessing the Coursera for Minnesota catalog and frequently asked questions, visit the Coursera for Minnesota site. UMN Office of Human Resources Contact Us 612-624-8647 or 800-756-2363 [email protected] For address and office hours, visit our OHR Directory . Intranets HR Community OHR Intranet OHR Operations HRMS Intranet Report Misconduct Report sexual misconduct, discrimination, or related retaliation. Report violations of University rules, regulations, and policies. This unit has systemwide responsibilities. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System . For Students, Faculty, and Staff One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff © 2026 Regents of the University of Minnesota . All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Privacy Statement Report Web Accessibility Issues Benefits Benefits Enrollment an