    "https://hr.umn.edu/jobs/Find-Job/Executive-Searches/Executive-Medical-Director-Boynton-Health": {
      "title": "Executive Medical Director",
      "description": "Executive Medical Director - Boynton Health | University of Minnesota Office of Human Resources Skip to main content Go to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities home page One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Office of Human Resources Jobs Why the UMN Benefits at UMN Relocation Assistance Find a Job Search UMN Jobs UMN Student Jobs Featured Positions U Services Positions Veterinary Technician Positions Executive Searches Associate Chancellor - Crookston Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth Executive Medical Director - Boynton Health Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management - UMN Morris Applicant Support Using the Job Application System Application and Interview Guidance UMN Graduate Assistant Job Guidance UMN Undergraduate Student Job Guidance Veteran Employment Guidance Contact Breadcrumb Home Find a Job Executive Searches Executive Medical Director - Boynton Health Executive Medical Director - Boynton Health Boynton Health is seeking a strong, accomplished clinical medical leader to serve as the executive medical director. This leader will champion student and patient-centered responsive healthcare through a team-based approach. This position will provide strategic direction and oversight for clinical services and collaborate with other leaders to foster, promote, and engage in health and wellness activities at Boynton and across the University of Minnesota Twin Cities campus. The executive medical director will leverage the clinic's strengths and demonstrate a commitment to innovation and effectiveness. Five Strong Campuses. One Strong State. The University of Minnesota System is one of the most comprehensive in the nation, with offerings to meet the interests of every student and the changing needs of our society. We're proud of our land-grant mission of world-class education, groundbreaking research, and our commitment to partnering with communities in our drive to serve Minnesota. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System. Learn more about our world-class benefits Contact Contact Anna Griebel at [email protected] with any questions about the position or location. Learn more about this role at the University Your browser does not support iframes, but you can visit Learn More Expand all Learn More + About Boynton Health Boynton Health is one of the largest and most comprehensive student health centers in the nation. With a legacy spanning over a century, the center is named in honor of its founding physician, Dr. Ruth Boynton. Today, Boynton Health provides care to 28,000 students and University staff through more than 85,000 visits annually. The clinic offers a wide array of services including urgent and preventive primary care, therapy and psychiatry, an eye clinic, a full-service pharmacy, physical therapy, nutritional counseling, and public health infectious disease management. Beyond basic medical care, Boynton Health is deeply committed to offering developmentally focused services that support students' holistic well-being, empowering them to achieve their highest educational goals. + Responsibilities This role is structured into two core areas of focus: Executive leadership (65%) Direct patient care in urgent and primary care (35%) This position supervises the clinical directors of primary care, psychiatry, optometry, allied health, and pharmacy. The executive medical director serves as a dyad with the executive director and reports directly to the executive vice president of health affairs. Executive Leadership (65%) Clinical Care Oversight and Supervision Oversee the development, review, and implementation of clinical guidelines, protocols, and evidence-based practice approaches. Direct the review and resolution of clinical concerns, patient grievances, medical errors, and infection prevention reports. Work closely with interdisciplinary teams to optimize patient care and improve workflow dynamics. Sponsor and champion upgrades to the Electronic Medical Record (EMR) and other technology systems to drive clinic efficiency. Cultivate collaborative relationships with local hospitals and external healthcare providers to streamline referral pathways, discharge planning, and continuity of care. Provide authoritative clinical consultation and expertise as needed during infectious disease outbreaks or campus-wide medical crises. Direct provider and staff supervision in alignment with the UMN’s performance management philosophy. Provide annual work plans, track metrics, conduct reviews, and deliver timely coaching and feedback to medical providers. Campus Public Health Response Design and execute clinical programs and services in coordination with the executive director to support the personal and public health needs of the University community. Lead clinical efforts and emergency preparedness in response to public health emergencies, infectious diseases, natural disasters, or student medical crises with the executive director. Actively liaise with local and state health agencies, the Office of Health Affairs, the Office for Student Affairs, and the Health Emergency Response Office (HERO), serving in Boynton's Incident Command Structure during emergencies. Quality and Safety Improvement Oversee, monitor, and meet defined clinical quality and safety metrics in partnership with the executive director. Initiate, champion, and sponsor annual clinical quality improvement projects. Actively participate in and lead committees dedicated to identifying and resolving patient and staff safety issues. Maintain readiness for the Accreditation Association for Ambulatory Health Care (AAAHC) by leading and supporting workflow updates that align with accreditation standards. Oversee clinical quality reviews and provider peer review processes, delegating a clinical leader to head the peer review committee. Model and enforce a strict commitment to patient privacy in compliance with state, federal (FERPA/HIPAA), and University regulations. Practice Leadership Attend and provide visible clinical leadership at service line and provider meetings. Guide and actively participate in clinical quality or interdisciplinary consultation meetings. Monitor and mentor providers in areas of responsibility, focusing on clinical performance, professional staff interactions, documentation standards, and collaborative behavior. Facilitate leadership and continuing professional development opportunities for clinical leaders and medical staff. Serve as the final authority on clinical policies, protocols, and guidelines governing practitioners (including physicians, physician assistants, and nurse practitioners). Ensure clinical directors under supervision develop, review, and revise policies to govern their respective practices. Partner with human resources to define clinical qualifications and competencies, leading the recruitment, interviewing, hiring, and onboarding of new providers and clinical directors. Engagement and Communication Establish and maintain positive, respectful, and collaborative relationships with patients, staff, and the executive team. Clearly communicate organizational goals, operational initiatives, and updates to clinical staff. Disseminate relevant clinical policy updates, guidelines, and procedural changes. Facilitate healthy interdisciplinary communication and actively manage conflict resolution. Respond to clinical concerns and feedback from campus stakeholders, including participating in Student Health Advisory Committee meetings. Direct Patient Care in Urgent and Primary Care (35%) The executive medical director maintains an active clinical practice. Privileges are granted annually according to Minnesota state law and include, but are not limited to: Taking patient histories and performing detailed physical examinations, including well-visits and preventive evaluations. Ordering, interpreting, and evaluating diagnostic data and laboratory tests. Performing diagnostic and therapeutic procedures within approved clinical privileges (e.g., biopsy, minor surgery, wound care). Prescribing, administering, and dispensing prescription and nonprescription medications and medical devices. Diagnosing and treating acute illnesses, infectious diseases, minor trauma, and chronic conditions or diseases. Issuing patient referrals to internal and external providers to facilitate treatment plans, including care coordination for severe mental illness. Providing contraceptive services, including emergency contraception. Educating patients on health promotion, disease prevention, current treatment options, and compliance, while addressing patient questions. Reviewing test results with patients via appointments, telephone consults, letters, or secure messages. Consulting with other physicians and healthcare professionals to confirm complex diagnoses and coordinate care plans. Mentoring and supervising the clinical work of nursing staff, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, and clinical learners. + Qualifications Required Qualifications MD or DO degree Unrestricted licensure (or immediate eligibility) by the State of Minnesota to practice medicine ABMS board certification in your medical specialty Active DEA certification Minimum of five (5) years of senior clinical management, leadership, and supervisory experience in an outpatient primary care group practice, community health clinic, and/or college student healthcare setting Demonstrated track record of building, nurturing, and leading high-performing clinical teams Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to handle difficult conversations and deliver clear objectives Deep proficiency in healthcare operations, clinic financial aspects, change management, and personnel management Comprehensive understanding of healthcare laws, regulations, and compliance standards Proven commitment to serving all patients and a thorough understanding of how social and economic determinants of health impact diverse campus communities Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a highly matrixed organization Demonstrated enterprise leadership capability Strong scientific and technological leadership Multilingual skills Intuitive creativity and a passion for healthcare innovation Deep commitment to student- and patient-centric care models High level of emotional intelligence (specifically self-awareness, self-management, social awareness, and relationship management) + Salary, Benefits, and Other Details Starting salary range: $265,000–325,000 (depending on education/qualifications/experience) Work arrangements: In person Benefits: As an employee with an academic professionals and administrators (P&A) classification, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package with low-cost health coverage, professional development opportunities, and retirement plan with 10% employer contribution. (See our benefits page for more information.) + Applications and Nominations Please submit a cover letter and a resume (or CV). Apply here Please submit application materials by August 31, 2026, for priority consideration. The position will remain open until filled. Coming in as a candidate for a position through the executive search process, and having led executive searches in past organizations, my own bar was fairly high. Questions were handled professionally and compassionately. The candidate experience overall was positive and affirming, and I felt I was in good hands throughout. -Autumn Amadou-Blegen, SPHR, SHRM-SCP Associate Vice Chancellor of Human Resources 2026 Best Employers for Company Culture, Forbes 80% Would recommend to a friend, Glassdoor #4 Best States, U.S. News An Equal Opportunity Employer The University of Minnesota shall provide equal access to and opportunity in its programs, facilities, and employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, gender, age, marital status, disability, public assistance status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. Talent Acquisition | UMN Office of Human Resources Contact Email: [email protected] Student Employment Email: [email protected] Quick Links Find a Job Comprehensive Benefits Using the Application System This unit has systemwide responsibilities. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System . For Students, Faculty, and Staff One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff © 2026 Regents of the University of Minnesota . All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Privacy Statement Report Web Accessibility Issues Benefits Benefits Enrollment and Changes Enrollment Overview Upcoming Benefits Changes How to Enroll New Employee or Newly Eligible Enrollment Open Enrollment Life Events Reclassification Year-Round Changes Leaving the UMN Leaving the UMN Overview Layoff Severance & Non-Renewal COBRA Continuation of Coverage Preparing for Retirement Medical Benefits Medical Plans Medica Plan Options Pharmacy Program Medication Therapy Management Convenience Care/Walk-in Clinics Virtual Care Travel Program Emergency Travel Program Diabetes Prevention & Management Dental Benefits Dental Plans Dental Plan Availability and Comparison Life and Disability Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Short-Term Disability Insurance Academic Disability Basic Life Insurance Additional Life Insurance Retirement Savings & Financial Counseling Retirement Savings Plans Overview Plan Comparison Financial Counseling and Resources Spending and Savings Accounts Flexible Spending Accounts (FSAs) Health Savings Accounts (HSAs) Leaves and Time Away Vacations, Time Away & Leaves University Holiday Calendars Vacation Paid Time Off Sick Time Off Leave of Absence Planning a Leave of Absence Types of Leave Minnesota Paid Leave Wellness and Family Care Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Family Resources Mental Health Resources Wellbeing Program About the Employee Wellbeing Program Wellbeing Program Frame